# Marker file only -- podman-docker's /usr/bin/docker wrapper tests for its
# existence, nothing reads the contents:
#
#   [ -e /etc/containers/nodocker ] || \
#   [ -e "${XDG_CONFIG_HOME-$HOME/.config}/containers/nodocker" ] || \
#     echo "Emulate Docker CLI using podman. ..." >&2
#
# Its presence silences that banner on every `docker ...` call. Kept here
# rather than at /etc/containers/nodocker so it is tracked and stowed per
# user instead of being untracked system state.
#
# Note there is no PODMAN_IGNORE_NODOCKER environment variable -- the wrapper
# only ever checks for these two files.
